/** @mainpage

This suite exercises tsf-systemd - reading the systemd state and
service-hardening posture of the Test Agent it runs on, over
libsystemd's sd-bus:

- @ref systemd-list - snapshot the units and read one active service's
  hardening properties (NoNewPrivileges, ProtectSystem, the capability
  bounding set, ...);
- @ref systemd-audit - read a set of services as a sandboxing posture
  through tsf-cybersec and log it.

It is read-only - it starts, stops and changes no unit. What units
exist is the host's to decide, so the suite asserts no particular unit:
a host without systemd skips cleanly, and the audit is informational
(a stock host runs many services with the systemd defaults).

*/
